# Per-element call in a non-map closed body — refused (besluit 1-A, lens round)

The ratified per-element 2-4 shape is an inline `(output of S with {…}).f` that
is DIRECTLY the map lambda body. Writing the same call directly inside a FOLD
reducer body (a natural `combine … with (acc + (output of Kamer with {…}).bedrag)`
instead of `map → fold`) also lands in a closed body — but not the map body. Its
`Invoke` would lower as a closed-body TERM of the reducer's `+`, which clingo's
`closed_term` cannot translate (only the map path lowers via `body_branches`), so
ref would compute while clingo TRANSLATION-FAULTs — a ref-only lowering. The gate
is `in_map_body` (the DIRECT map body), not the broader `in_body`, so this shape
is refused per element. Own-authored, rights-free.

```catala
declaration scope Kamer:
  input grondslag content integer
  output bedrag content integer

scope Kamer:
  definition bedrag equals grondslag + 100

declaration scope Aanslag:
  input grondslagen content list of integer
  output totaal content integer

scope Aanslag:
  definition totaal equals
    combine all g
      among grondslagen
      in acc initially 0 with (acc + (output of Kamer with { -- grondslag: g }).bedrag)
```
